    (1778251562597, "The movement of air in and out of the body to maintain appropriate concentrations of O2 and CO2. The primary, central, control is the brainstem. It senses pH — with acidosis, or a decrease in pH, rate/depth of breathing increase to correct it. Secondary, peripheral, control is PaO₂ \"sensors\" in the aortic arch. Decreased PaO₂ = hypoxemia, which results in increase in rate/depth of breathing.", "What is ventilation? Primary and secondary control?"),
